<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Student Work on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/student-work/</link><description>Recent content in Student Work on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 25 Jan 2010 16:28:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/student-work/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fracmetrica Black .otf</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66644/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Jan 2010 16:28:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66644/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;if you like modern and geometric fonts and blackletter as well, have a look at the typophile post &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317083205/http:/typophile.com/node/66643"&gt;»Fracmetrica Black .otf«&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fracmetrica Black .otf</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66643/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Jan 2010 16:23:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66643/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;the free-font &lt;strong&gt;»Fracmetrica Black«&lt;/strong&gt; is a modern and geometric blackletter with several opentype-features like ligatures, case-sensitives, text figures.&lt;br&gt;
It&amp;rsquo;s kind of condensed and has a high contrast. The typeface&amp;rsquo;s construction is based on an isometric 60°-grid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349im_/http:/typophile.com/files/jakob_p2_fracmetrica_intro_3878.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Created by Jakob Runge 2009 during the &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349/http:/gestaltung.fh-wuerzburg.de/blogs/werk_statt_villa/?cat=6"&gt;Workshop »fancy_fonts_&amp;amp;_porno_pattern« at the university of applied sciences würzburg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349im_/http:/typophile.com/files/jakob_fracmetrica2_style_1_4071.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349im_/http:/typophile.com/files/jakob_fracmetrica2_zeichen_5447.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the open-type version of »Fracmetrica Black« is for free creative-commons download.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349/http:/gestaltung.fh-wuerzburg.de/blogs/werk_statt_villa/?p=462"&gt;about the finished and digitalised font&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349/http:/gestaltung.fh-wuerzburg.de/blogs/werk_statt_villa/?p=372"&gt;sketches and work in progess&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414142349/http:/issuu.com/werk_statt_villa/docs/werk-impuls/107"&gt;fracmetrica black in the »WERK imPuls« magazine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>In progress casual upright script</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65526/</link><pubDate>Sun, 20 Dec 2009 11:29:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65526/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Reposting from &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150419144420/http:/www.typophile.com/node/61411"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. This is my first font. It needs lots of work (especially the caps, although I&amp;rsquo;ve finally got a plan for them!) but I&amp;rsquo;d love some feedback in the meantime.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150419144420im_/http:/typophile.com/files/retroupright_5553.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gilly&lt;/p&gt;
